EQUIVALENT: url: credentials in the authority are accepted
    unreachable: without the `@` check `_host_of` keeps `user:pass@data.example`, then splits on `:` and returns `user` - a single label, which the two-label minimum in `_admissible` refuses. The check stays because returning the empty string says 'this has no host I will trust' rather than quietly inventing one.
EQUIVALENT: url: localhost is accepted
    unreachable: `localhost` is a single label, and `_admissible` requires at least two. The named check stays because it is the one a reader looks for, and because the label rule below it is one edit away from admitting a bare name.
